From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:38:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse unblock while a spend decision is pending
 [daveey]

Problem: unblock reported released for a spend-held triage card, then the
next dispatch tick silently restored triage.
Why: unblock accepted triage without consulting the durable spend decision.
Why: only promoted_manual/archive acknowledge that decision; unblocked does
not, so status alone was not release authority.
Why invisible: the pending-decision hold branch updated status without an
event. Existing release and spend tests did not compose these paths.
Root: release acknowledgement and dispatcher eligibility used different
policy checks. Keep the recorded-decision contract, rather than expanding
ordinary unblock into spend authorization.

Refuse in the existing transaction-owned unblock guard; share promotion
guidance with CLI/tool/operator consumers and supervisor resume preflight.
Record spend_budget_held only when the pending branch actually flips status.
Do not emit another spend-stop episode or duplicate events on idle ticks.

Proof: regression suite RED on unchanged main (five failures), GREEN with
seven tests including supervisor request/drain interleaving. Existing spend,
release and tool tests: 85 passed; supervisor batch: 35 passed; broader
consumer batch: 294 passed (overlapping batches). Three mutations killed:
unblock guard removal, unconditional hold event, supervisor preflight bypass.
scripts/check: all 20 checks pass. No live task mutations.

